<title>USA: Armey sees 25 Republicans against US spending bill.</title>
<headline>Armey sees 25 Republicans against US spending bill.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>House Majority Leader Richard Armey said about 25 House Republicans would likely vote against the spending bill mainly because of a tobacco tax increase.</p>
<p>But the Texas Republican expected almost all the House Republicans to vote for the five-year tax cut bill.</p>
<p>The House and Senate were expected to vote on the spending bill Wednesday and on the tax bill Thursday, Armey said.</p>
</text>
